Adsorption on WB<sub>5-x</sub> surfaces

Structural condigurations of different gas molecules adsorbed on the surfaces of higher tungsten boride WB<sub>5-x</sub>

There are two folders corresponding to (010) and (101) surfaces. The name of each file is `molecule_[number_of_configuration]_ surface_[initial/final].vasp`.

So `CO_1_101_initial.vasp` means that this structure for initial position of CO molecule in configuration 1 on the (101) surface of WB<sub>5-x</sub>.

These structures can be used for DFT calculations and further training of model to calcualte adsorption or perform large-scale simulations.

---


By using this model please cite our paper

[A. D. Radina, V. S. Baidyshev, I. V. Chepkasov, N. A. Matsokin, T. Altalhi, B. I. Yakobson, and A. G. Kvashnin, Theoretical study of adsorption properties and CO oxidation reaction on surfaces of higher tungsten boride, Sci Rep ​**14**​, 12788 (2024).](https://https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-63676-7)
